hat the lead stayed comfortable."}, {"turn": 42, "text": "J2 lost 30.7 points, GPT-6.1 Sol's worst move, sending Black's lead from +41.3 to +72.0. The engine's choice was D8. It started a long swap: White's H4, J4 and H3 each lost between 28.9 and 30.2 points, while Black's replies each lost 28.9 to 30.0."}, {"turn": 47, "text": "Black's J3 lost 30.0 points, the 20k's worst move, and returned the lead from +72.8 to +42.8. The engine wanted D8. By now White's stones ran along row 4 and Black's along row 5 on the right side, and both sides kept handing the same large swing back and forth."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "The `inspect` function (and `current-position-liberties.js`) only parsed the current board, listed chains and liberties, and computed the captures and resulting chain for one move the player had already named. The other scripts replayed the actual game record, kept the allocation notes, wrote game-082.md/.sgf and AGENTS.md, and called `play`; none of them looped over candidate moves or looked ahead.", "stop": false}}